# The desktop's own answer to "what opens this?", which is what xdg-open, GIO
# and the xdg-desktop-portal consult. It is therefore what Firefox's "open
# containing folder", a file chooser's "show in folder", and anything else that
# hands a directory to the desktop will reach.
#
# yazi rather than Dolphin, matching SUPER+E in hypr/keybinds.lua. yazi is a
# TUI, so applications/yazi.desktop is where the argument actually lands: a
# kitty window running yazi.
#
# install.sh symlinks this file into ~/.config. xdg-mime dereferences a symlink
# when it edits one, so `xdg-mime default ...` rewrites this file rather than
# replacing the link -- expect such an edit to show up here to commit.
#
# The jetbrains:// handler is the JetBrains Toolbox's, kept because taking the
# whole file over would otherwise drop it.
[Default Applications]
inode/directory=yazi.desktop
x-scheme-handler/jetbrains=jetbrainsd.desktop
